    <string name="tunnel_multihop_desc">Multi-hop routes traffic through a separate entry relay so the exit never sees your IP. Warren on Android always connects multi-hop: a distinct entry relay forwards your traffic to the chosen exit, so the "Multihop" indicator is shown while connected.</string>
    <string name="tunnel_obfuscation_title">HTTP/3 mimicry obfuscation is always-on for Warren tunnels.</string>
    <string name="tunnel_obfuscation_desc">Warren tunnels masquerade as standard browser HTTP/3 traffic: ALPN h3, SNI warrenbrowse.com, Initial-packet split, UDP/443. This is not togglable because disabling it would make Warren clients immediately recognisable on the network.</string>
